international regions with market insights.\n\nMain activities\n\n Become Market Intelligence savy! Study market intelligence to be able to identify, recommend and challenge the regions on segment/ vertical strategic focus \n Engage with International Sales & Marketing to define insights & recommendation to support our revenue and GM ambition (grow, keep, expand...), marketing by vertical, revenue by vertical, which accts? which new logos? look at TML.... \n Facilitate consumption of market intelligence data: inspire and teach the OBI Sales & Marketing team \n Share and present data insights to a larger OBI audience (in the future) and act as the senior data expert for OBI \n Contribute to the strategy/planning process by providing market data \n\nResponsibilities\n\n About you \n\nMarket Intelligence vs Marketing\n\n Marketing campaigns are centrally managed by Marketing teams \n Market insights requests are documented and scoped by Marketing teams \n Market insights are provided and shared by Market Intelligence \n Market intelligence is not in charge of the Marketing plan, Budget plan or Strategic Plan. However, Market Intelligence should have an understanding of these plans, with a clear demand to come with proactive insights where relevant \n Delivery of market studies, market targeting, or campaign input is done by Market intelligence and delivered to the (regional) Marketing SPOC \n The target process includes the need to document each campaign in the CRM, allowing us to trace follow-up and commercial performance \n\nMarket Intelligence vs Business Intelligence\n\n Market intelligence applies market data to provide marketing recommendations, this is done for prospects or customers, \n Business intelligence provides commercial reporting, order tracking and revenue reporting \n Marketing Intelligence will rely on customer data provided by the BI team (Customer Base Mngt, commercial performance, order tracking\u2026) \n\nKey Knowledge and Abilities:\n\n understanding of Orange Business strategy and solutions/portfolio \n understanding of International customers and its business buildup \n understanding market & sales intelligence and facilitate embedding this in the Marketing plan \n ability to animate the main users of the market data intelligence \n\nKey Skills: \n\nMandatory skills: \n\n Proven proficiency in Data Analytics (using preferably Tableau but other BI tools are acceptable - Tableau, QlikSense/QlikView, Looker, etc.) \n Proficiency in data modelling & automation (ETL, ELT, creating & maintaining data pipelines) \n Data Science/ML Engineering background - understanding statistical models & implementing suitable ML models for different UCs (supervised vs unsupervised modelling), programming language - preferably Python (pandas, numpy, scikit-learn, etc.) \n Proficiency in Business analytics -> full E2E delivery \n Solid stakeholder & project management skills \n\nOptional Skills\n\n Agile frameworks (SAFe, LEAN, etc.) \n Knowledge of Scrum/Kanban \n Knowledge of CI/CD best practices (GIT - GitLab, Sourcetree, etc.) \n CRM systems (SFDC is preferred but understanding CRM data governance is a plus) \n\nBase salary from 2 410 \u20ac brutto per month, actual salary is likely to be higher based on skills, knowledge and experience.\n\nYou bring rigor, passion for challenges, and determination. You seek the opportunity to expand your expertise, achieve your goals, and thrive.", "lastUpdate": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "referralName": "", "referralContact": "", "referralStatus": "", "resumeFileId": "1uBi5ifbUn7snBzU83GiMgD4kavwnrqv-", "resumeUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clFileId": "", "clUrl": "", "sections": {"summary": "<p>Senior Data &amp; Business Analyst combining extensive enterprise data analytics and operations intelligence experience with a strong foundation in commercial strategy and stakeholder consulting. Proven track record of utilizing <strong>SQL, Python, and Tableau</strong> to diagnose operational SLA bottlenecks, standardize cross-functional workflows, and scale process efficiency across global teams. Adept at applying <strong>workflow automation and QA governance</strong> and <strong>narrative insight synthesis</strong> to translate complex datasets into clear executive presentations and actionable business decisions.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Data Analysis &amp; Database Management:</strong> Python (Pandas, Numpy), Api/data Integration, Database Management, SQL (Postgresql, Mysql, Bigquery), R, Excel, Jupyter Notebooks</li>\n  <li><strong>Business Intelligence &amp; Visualization:</strong> Dashboard/report Automation, Tableau, Narrative Insight Synthesis, Interactive Dashboards, Executive Presentations, KPI Scorecard Design</li>\n  <li><strong>Data Governance &amp; Process Optimization:</strong> Data Transformation, Data Cleaning &amp; Wrangling, Identifying Improvement Opportunities, Quality Assurance, Automating Workflows (n8n), Root-cause &amp; Variance Analysis</li>\n  <li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration &amp; Strategy:</strong> Stakeholder Communication, Cross-functional Teamwork, Business Acumen, Consulting &amp; Client Engagement, Training &amp; Mentorship, Critical Thinking &amp; Problem Solving</li>\n</ul>", "exp1_bullets": "<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Spearheaded end-to-end <strong>SQL data modelling</strong> and pipeline optimization across 1M+ monthly records using Python and BigQuery, cutting manual reporting overhead by 40%.</li>\n    <li>Designed and deployed interactive <strong>Tableau dashboards</strong> and automated KPI reporting suites across 15+ cross-functional launches, accelerating leadership decision cycles.</li>\n    <li>Conducted deep-dive <strong>root-cause analysis</strong> and customer segmentation across multi-source datasets, partnering with engineering and business teams to maintain 95% delivery quality.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Built automated <strong>performance analytics</strong> trackers and Excel/SQL competency matrices across 200+ specialists, boosting new-hire quality scores by 84% within two quarters.</li>\n    <li>Led <strong>diagnostic gap analysis</strong> on operational SLA and quality telemetry, redesigning process workflows to reduce recurring knowledge and execution gaps by 30%.</li>\n    <li>Partnered with global operations stakeholders on <strong>capacity planning</strong> and workflow standardization, driving a 25% increase in team productivity and throughput.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Customer Support Representative, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2021 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager at Orange Business,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Senior Business Analyst role at Orange Business. With over five years of hands-on experience building reliable SQL and Python reporting pipelines, designing executive Tableau dashboards, and partnering with product and operations leaders, I am eager to contribute immediately to Orange Business's data and analytics goals.</p>\n<p>Throughout my career across high-volume operational and business intelligence environments, I have focused on turning complex, fragmented datasets into clear, trustworthy decision frameworks. Whether automating recurring ETL workflows or establishing governed KPI definitions across teams, I prioritize data accuracy and practical business impact.</p>\n<p>In my recent work, I re-engineered manual reporting workflows into automated SQL and Tableau pipelines that reduced reporting latency by over 40% while uncovering key drivers of funnel conversion and SLA performance. This blend of technical execution and stakeholder communication aligns closely with what Orange Business seeks in this position.</p>\n<p>I thrive in fast-paced environments where requirements evolve quickly and cross-functional clarity is essential. My background spans end-to-end requirement gathering, UAT governance, root-cause diagnostics, and translating technical findings for non-technical leadership.</p>\n<p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in SQL, Python, Tableau, and business analysis can support Orange Business's upcoming initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "3", "sNoNum": 3, "resumeId": "14bb0752-5e6b-4d74-8890-f93999448a0a", "company": "Atlys", "industry": "Travel Tech / Consumer FinTech", "jobId": "N/A", "title": "Senior Data Analyst", "jd": "The Role\nWe\u2019re looking for a Senior Data Analyst to own critical business data end to end and help teams make better decisions with it.\n\nYou\u2019ll build the metrics, dashboards and analyses that become the single source of truth across the business, while partnering closely with teams to solve high-impact problems and uncover growth opportunities.\n\nThis role is for someone who can independently navigate messy data, define the right questions, and turn analysis into clear decisions and action.\n\nThe Job\nOwn business data as a reliable source of truth by ensuring key metrics, reports and dashboards are accurate, consistent and trusted across teams.\n\nBuild and evolve decision-making systems across business, marketing, finance and other core functions through dashboards, reporting and analytical frameworks.\n\nTurn complex datasets into actionable insights by writing advanced SQL, analysing large datasets, and identifying trends, anomalies and opportunities.\n\nDefine the metrics that matter by partnering with teams to establish KPIs, improve measurement and create clarity around performance.\n\nLead data-driven problem solving by independently structuring ambiguous business questions, diagnosing root causes and recommending actions that improve outcomes.\n\nThe Ideal Candidate\nYou\u2019ll likely thrive in this role if you:\n\nHave 3-6 years of experience in data analytics, business analytics or a similar role, ideally in a fast-moving consumer or technology business.\n\nAre exceptionally strong in SQL and comfortable independently working with large, complex and imperfect datasets.\n\nHave strong experience with visualisation tools such as Tableau, Tableau, Looker Studio or Metabase, and can build dashboards that drive decisions rather than just report numbers.\n\nBring strong analytical and business judgment, with the ability to structure ambiguous problems and translate analysis into clear recommendations for stakeholders.\n\nHave exposure to Python or a strong understanding of how data flows through products and technology systems.", "location": "Delhi HQ", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://www.atlys.com/careers", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Not Created", "combinedDocStatus": "To be reviewed", "appliedOn": "8/10/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/10/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "", "hrEmail": "", "hrPhone": "", "reviewerNotes": "", "clNotes": "", "generalNotes": "", "aboutCompany": "Fast-growing visa & travel technology platform.", "resumeDriveId": "14N5d0U6Lq2GILIIBB3ZZdltuaW2Cm1pI", "resumeLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "resumePreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clDriveId": "", "clLink": "", "clPreviewUrl": "", "roleCategory": "finance_fpa_analyst", "extractedKeywords": "[object Object]", "revisionCount": 1, "clRevisionCount": 1, "resumeSections": {"summary_html": "<p>Senior Data &amp; Business Analyst combining extensive enterprise data analytics and operations intelligence experience with a strong foundation in commercial strategy and stakeholder consulting. Proven track record of architecting automated data pipelines and interactive KPI reporting suites using <strong>SQL, Python, and Tableau</strong> to streamline reporting workflows, resolve operational bottlenecks, and elevate cross-functional delivery quality. Adept at applying <strong>data cleaning and transformation</strong> and <strong>diagnostic root-cause analysis</strong> to translate complex datasets into clear executive presentations and actionable business decisions.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong