igning executive Tableau dashboards, and partnering with product and operations leaders, I am eager to contribute immediately to Atlys's data and analytics goals.</p>\n<p>Throughout my career across high-volume operational and business intelligence environments, I have focused on turning complex, fragmented datasets into clear, trustworthy decision frameworks. Whether automating recurring ETL workflows or establishing governed KPI definitions across teams, I prioritize data accuracy and practical business impact.</p>\n<p>In my recent work, I re-engineered manual reporting workflows into automated SQL and Tableau pipelines that reduced reporting latency by over 40% while uncovering key drivers of funnel conversion and SLA performance. This blend of technical execution and stakeholder communication aligns closely with what Atlys seeks in this position.</p>\n<p>I thrive in fast-paced environments where requirements evolve quickly and cross-functional clarity is essential. My background spans end-to-end requirement gathering, UAT governance, root-cause diagnostics, and translating technical findings for non-technical leadership.</p>\n<p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in SQL, Python, Tableau, and business analysis can support Atlys's upcoming initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "4", "sNoNum": 4, "resumeId": "63d01cf5-6623-4ac7-bc4c-7505d13fecdb", "company": "Turing", "industry": "AI & Global Engineering Talent Cloud", "jobId": "N/A", "title": "Technical Business Analyst", "jd": "About the Role\nTuring is seeking a Technical Business Analyst who can operate comfortably in two worlds at once: the day-to-day realities of Operations and Finance, and the practical constraints of building software. This is a role for someone who listens deeply, asks sharp questions, maps real workflows, and translates that understanding into clear, testable requirements that engineering teams can deliver with confidence.\n\nYou'll join a global team supporting a leading alternative investment manager with more than 30 years of proven expertise across Private Equity, Credit, and Real Assets. The business is known for its integrated platform, strong investment performance, value-oriented philosophy, and its people. You'll work closely with business stakeholders, product owners, and engineers to reduce ambiguity, improve shared understanding, and accelerate delivery \u2014 without sacrificing quality or control.\n\nWhat You'll Do\nLead discovery with stakeholders to understand current-state workflows, pain points, controls, and desired outcomes.\nDistill ambiguity into clarity by writing crisp problem statements, scope boundaries, assumptions, risks, and success measures.\nTranslate business needs into delivery-ready artifacts: process flows, user stories, acceptance criteria, and non-functional requirements.\nPartner with engineers and product owners to refine requirements, resolve tradeoffs, and keep execution unblocked.\nSupport testing and validation by defining test scenarios, helping coordinate UAT, and ensuring delivered features match intent.\nMaintain traceability: align requirements to outcomes and support auditability where needed (controls, approvals, data lineage).\nUse AI tools responsibly to accelerate analysis and documentation \u2014 summarization, drafting, comparison, and gap analysis \u2014 while validating accuracy and protecting sensitive information.\nCommunicate clearly and consistently, sharing status, decisions, and open questions in a way that builds trust.\nWhat We're Looking For\n8+ years experience as a business analyst or similar experience leading business analysis or requirements work on real software delivery projects. \nStrong discovery and requirements skills \u2014 you move from conversations to structured, testable requirements quickly.\nComfort in technical discussions: APIs, data flows, basic system behavior, and knowing the right questions to ask engineers.\nExcellent written communication \u2014 your artifacts are clear, concise, and immediately usable by both engineering and business partners.\nStrong stakeholder management \u2014 you build rapport, handle conflict professionally, and create alignment without force.\nThe ability to think in workflows and data: process mapping, edge cases, exceptions, and operational controls.\nHigh integrity and maturity \u2014 you are transparent, consistent, and trusted, especially under pressure.\nAn independent operator who can own a project end to end with minimal oversight.\nNice to Have\nExperience in back office operations, finance, accounting, or control-oriented domains (reconciliations, reporting, hand-offs, approvals).\nFamiliarity with agile delivery (stories, backlogs, iteration planning), while staying comfortable in less mature environments.\nExperience working with data stores and queries (SQL basics), or partnering on reporting and analytics needs.\nExposure to event-driven or workflow-based systems (messaging, orchestration) and an understanding of how these affect requirements and audit trails.", "location": "hybrid on-site in New York, New York", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://careers.turing.com/roles", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Ready for Review", "combinedDocStatus": "To be reviewed", "appliedOn": "8/25/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/25/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-06 09:00 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "", "hrEmail": "", "hrPhone": "", "reviewerNotes": "", "clNotes": "", "generalNotes": "", "aboutCompany": "AI-powered technology services and talent platform.", "resumeDriveId": "1x9TYlpeTRP5-fxiqjbwhR2ivstKQUruo", "resumeLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "resumePreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clDriveId": "1-pSNu7d4lV0jIdNsxSEUYLzI7equaBOl", "clLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/