ity by 84% via <strong>user stories &amp; acceptance criteria</strong>.</li>\n    <li>Deployed self-serve operational metrics using <strong>stakeholder management</strong> strategies, closing knowledge gaps by 30% and lifting team productivity by 25%.</li>\n    <li>Facilitated <strong>UAT coordination</strong> and <strong>agile delivery</strong> cycles for internal HR tools, ensuring rigorous compliance and <strong>auditability &amp; controls</strong> standards.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2010 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed end-to-end client engagements focusing on <strong>finance &amp; accounting</strong> structures, scaling HORECA sector sales by 25% through strategic channel alignment.</li>\n    <li>Streamlined digital campaign architectures by translating ambiguous client requests into precise development tasks, accelerating customer acquisition velocity by 30%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<div class=\"letter-meta\">\n  <div class=\"letter-date\">September 29, 2026</div>\n  <div class=\"recipient-block\">\n    <div>Hiring Team</div><div>Turing</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"subject-line\"><strong>Subject: Application for the Technical Business Analyst Role</strong></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Technical Business Analyst role at Turing. What stood out to me in the job description is the focus on turning messy day-to-day operations into clean requirements and clear reports. Before spending the last five years in data analytics, I ran my own small marketing agency for ten years. That mix taught me how much time teams lose when numbers do not match across different tools. Fixing those gaps between business users and engineering is the part of the job I enjoy most.</p>\n<p>Outside of writing SQL queries and building Tableau dashboards, I spend my free time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating small daily tasks with n8n. Growing mushrooms in North India is not a fancy hobby. It comes down to watching basic details closely. If moisture or airflow slips even a little, the whole batch fails. I bring that same habit to my work when I check data quality, map workflows, or build reports that leaders rely on.</p>\n<p>I also believe analysis is only useful when it solves a real problem on the ground. At Concentrix, our hiring data showed that new joiners were struggling once they started work. Sending another dashboard to management was not fixing the issue. I looked closely at the hiring steps and worked with leadership to bring our training team directly into the interview stage. That simple change improved hire quality by 84 percent. In my current role at Highspring India, I use the same practical approach across four engineering teams to automate recurring reports and cut manual work by 40 percent.</p>\n<p>My day-to-day work covers SQL, Python, Tableau, and working closely with business and tech teams. If the team at Turing uses an internal tool I have not worked with yet, I learn new systems quickly. Practical challenges early in my career taught me how to stay resourceful, focus on the basics, and get things done without hand-holding. When I take ownership of a task, nobody has to follow up twice.</p>\n<p>I would welcome the chance to bring this steady, practical approach to Turing. Thank you for your time and consideration, and I look forward to speaking with you soon.</p>"}, {"sNo": "5", "sNoNum": 5, "resumeId": "RES-5", "company": "Stripe", "industry": "Payments", "jobId": "N/A", "title": "Payments Analyst", "jd": "As a Technical Operations Analyst on the Payments team, you will own the reliability and accuracy of some of the world's most critical payment flows, a platform processing hundreds of billions of dollars annually. You will sit at the intersection of engineering, finance, and operations: triaging live payment failures, driving reconciliation accuracy, and partnering with financial institutions globally to resolve issues fast.\n\nThis is not a passive monitoring role. You will be expected to independently own investigations end-to-end, identify systemic issues before they escalate, and drive process improvements that scale with Stripe's growth.\n\nResponsibilities\nOwn reconciliation and payments-related investigations, ensuring accurate ledgering of funds and resolving discrepancies with banking partners swiftly and precisely.\nProactively monitor payment performance across users and payment methods; triage degradation alerts, diagnose root causes, and communicate findings clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders.\nServe as the escalation point for complex support inquiries from Technical Account Managers, Product Support, and internal Stripe teams providing fast, well-reasoned resolutions.\nInterface directly with Stripe's global financial partners (card networks, banks, payment processors) to manage operational incidents and drive resolution.\nValidate the accuracy of Stripe's financial data through rigorous analysis and cross-functional collaboration with finance and infrastructure engineering teams.\nIdentify process inefficiencies and lead automation initiatives to reduce manual workload and improve operational throughput at scale.\nBuild and maintain high-quality SOPs, runbooks, and process documentation to ensure institutional knowledge is captured and transferable.\nWho you are\nWe're looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.\n\nMinimum requirements\n3-7 years of experience in a technical operations, payments operations, or financial technology role.\nAdvanced SQL proficiency - you write complex queries (joins, window functions, aggregations) independently and use them as a primary tool for investigation and root cause analysis.\nDeep understanding of end-to-end payment flows - including authorization, clearing, settlement, reconciliation, and exception handling across multiple payment methods and geographies.\nDemonstrated experience investigating and resolving high-severity operational incidents in a payments or financial systems environment with minimal oversight.\nStrong experience working with large-scale financial datasets - validating accuracy, identifying anomalies, and reconciling discrepancies across systems.\nProven ability to manage complex, cross-functional workflows - coordinating simultaneously with engineering, finance, banking partners, and business teams.\nTrack record of identifying process gaps and driving automation or efficiency improvements that meaningfully reduced manual workload.\nExperience writing and maintaining SOPs, runbooks, and technical documentation to a high standard.\nExcellent written and verbal communication in English - able to translate complex technical issues into clear, concise updates for both technical and non-technical audiences.\nComfortable operating with high autonomy in a fast-paced environment, managing competing priorities and time-sensitive deadlines without close supervision.\nPreferred qualifications\nHands-on experience working directly with card networks, acquiring banks, or payment processors, including managing operational escalations and SLA-driven communications.\nExperience with payment cost optimization\nDeep understanding of end-to-end payment flows - including authorization, clearing, settlement, reconciliation, and exception handling across multiple payment methods and geographies.\nFamiliarity with accounting and financial reconciliation principles\nPrior experience in a high-growth fintech or global payments company operating at significant transaction scale.\nExperience building or improving monitoring and alerting frameworks for payment systems.\nPractical history of developing AI-driven solutions designed to automate and optimize high-volume operational workflows.", "location": "Bengaluru", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://stripe.com/careers/search", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Not Created", "combinedDocStatus": "To be reviewed", "appliedOn": "8/25/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/25/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-06 09:00 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "", "hrEmail": "", "hrPhone": "", "reviewerNotes": "", "clNotes": "", "generalNotes": "", "aboutCompany": "Global financial infrastructure platform for businesses.", "resumeDriveId": "1SD9swM8eobugH7LB-cYh6cEdBHWNWviU", "resumeLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "resumePreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clDriveId": "", "clLink": "", "clPreviewUrl": "", "roleCategory": "payments_operations_analyst", "extractedKeywords": "[object Object]", "revisionCount": 1, "clRevisionCount": 1, "resumeSections": {"summary_html": "<p>Payments Analyst combining a B.Comm in Finance with large-scale operations experience at Google and Concentrix to manage complex <strong>financial reconciliation</strong> and payment flows. Expert in utilizing <strong>advanced SQL</strong> for data validation, anomaly detection, and root cause analysis across global transaction ledgers. Committed to driving operational efficiency and cross-functional incident management to ensure the reliability of high-volume <strong>fintech operations</strong> at Stripe scale.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Data Analysis & Database Management:</strong> PostgreSQL, MySQL, BigQuery, Python (Pandas, NumPy), Excel</li>\n  <li><strong>Process Optimization & Data Governance:</strong> Automating wor