ire quality by 84%.</li>\n    <li>Deployed self-serve operational dashboards to streamline <strong>cross-functional collaboration</strong>, reducing stakeholder knowledge gaps by 30% and increasing productivity by 25%.</li>\n    <li>Delivered <strong>client-facing</strong> presentations and training modules that enforced strict adherence to operating rigor and compliance guidelines for 200+ team members.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2010 \u2013 Mar 2020</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Facilitated detailed <strong>contract review</strong> and vendor negotiations to protect profit margins and accelerate enterprise revenue growth across 50+ client accounts.</li>\n    <li>Optimized end-to-end operational workflows and resource allocation, successfully scaling agency output by 35% through enhanced <strong>operating rigor</strong>.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<p class=\"salutation\"><strong>To the Hiring Team at Stripe,</strong></p>\n<p>What caught my attention about the <strong>Financial Analyst, Business F&S</strong> role at Stripe is how directly the job description targets the messy reality of scaling financial operations: establishing clean, consistent reporting foundations and bringing rigorous standardization to opex, headcount, and month-end workflows. Having spent the last several years translating complex operational data into reliable financial insights\u2014preceded by a decade running my own commercial agency\u2014I know that most strategic friction happens when data hygiene breaks down between disparate systems. That operational intersection is precisely where I do my best work.</p>\n<p>When I am not profiling millions of records or building reporting dashboards, I spend my spare time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating personal workflows with <strong>n8n</strong>. Cultivating mushrooms in North India's climate isn't a romantic hobby; it is an exercise in strict variable control\u2014if humidity, airflow, or substrate prep drifts even slightly, the batch fails. I bring that same rigorous stewardship to financial systems, whether I am building <strong>standardized dashboards and data packs</strong> for leadership, running opex budget-versus-actual analysis, or driving <strong>cross-system data integrity</strong> across planning tools.</p>\n<p>Furthermore, I believe analysis is only as useful as the operational fix it drives. During my time at Concentrix, our workforce data kept flagging quality drops in new cohorts, and simply sending leadership another dashboard wasn't fixing it. I dug into the operational funnel, traced the disconnect between initial screening and floor realities, and made the case to embed our training team directly into the recruitment workflow. That structural adjustment drove an <strong>84% improvement in hire quality</strong>\u2014similar to how I now partner across <strong>4+ engineering and business groups</strong> at Highspring India to cut manual reporting overhead by 40% and resolve hundreds of data consistency issues.</p>\n<p>While my background covers strong ground across SQL, Python, Tableau, and financial data modeling, I may not have hands-on experience with every proprietary enterprise tool in your stack on day one. Early in my career, navigating real-world constraints taught me how to be resourceful, focus on fundamentals, and become a <strong>dedicated learner with a sharp focus</strong> on what actually moves the needle. Above all, I am <strong>unconditionally dependable</strong>\u2014when I take ownership of a financial deliverable, you will never have to chase me to see it through.</p>\n<p>I would value the chance to bring this grounded ownership, systems thinking, and steady execution to your F&S team.</p><p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to discussing how my experience can support Stripe's upcoming financial and operational initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "8", "sNoNum": 8, "resumeId": "RES-8", "company": "United", "industry": "Airlines", "jobId": "GGN00002639", "title": "Analyst - Data Scientist", "jd": "Description\nUnited's Digital Technology team is comprised of many talented individuals all working together with cutting-edge technology to build the best airline in the history of aviation. Our team designs, develops and maintains massively scaling technology solutions brought to life with innovative architectures, data analytics, and digital solutions.\n\n \n\nJob Overview and Responsibilities\n\nThe Data Scientist designs, develops, and implements scalable AI and Generative AI solutions that improve customer experience, business efficiency, and decision-making. The role builds production-grade applications and workflows using Python, SQL, large language models, Retrieval-Augmented Generation, and agentic AI frameworks. It applies advanced analysis, prompt engineering, evaluation, and observability practices to deliver reliable and useful AI capabilities. The role partners with cross-functional teams to translate ambiguous business needs into practical solutions and clearly communicate findings and recommendations.       \n\n \n\n\u2022    Design, develop, test, and deploy robust AI and Generative AI solutions that improve customer experience, operational efficiency, and business decision-making. \n\u2022    Build and deploy production-grade workflows, applications, and data pipelines using Python, SQL, relational databases, and modern AI tools. \n\u2022    Perform advanced exploratory analysis and feature engineering across structured and unstructured datasets to support scalable AI and Generative AI use cases. \n\u2022    Implement prompt engineering strategies, conduct LLM experiments, and apply output evaluation frameworks to ensure quality, relevance, accuracy, safety, and business usefulness.\n\u2022    Develop and scale Retrieval-Augmented Generation pipelines and integrate agentic AI frameworks for multi-step reasoning and workflow automation. \n\u2022    Implement AI observability and MLOps practices to monitor model behavior and system reliability; collaborate with cross-functional teams and communicate findings, risks, and recommendations to stakeholders. \n \n\n \n\n\nThis position is offered on local terms and conditions.  Expatriate assignments and sponsorship for employment visas, even on a time-limited visa status, will not be awarded. This position is for United Airlines Business Services Pvt. Ltd - a wholly owned subsidiary of United Airlines Inc.\n \n\nQualifications\nWhat\u2019s needed to succeed (Minimum Qualifications):\n\u2022    Candidates must hold a Master of Science or equivalent postgraduate degree in a STEM field.\n\u2022    Data Science, Statistics, Engineering, Computer Science, Operations Research, or a related STEM field. \n\u2022    1\u20132 years of industry experience in AI engineering, data science, analytics, or machine learning, including practical experience moving models or analytical workflows toward production. \n\u2022    Strong Python and SQL proficiency; software engineering fundamentals, including Git; experience with large relational datasets and platforms such as Microsoft SQL Server, Snowflake, BigQuery, or Teradata; practical knowledge of LLMs, prompt engineering, embeddings, RAG, and agentic AI; AI observability and MLOps; strong analytical problem-solving; ability to create clear Excel and PowerPoint presentations\n\u2022    Exhibit strong spoken and written communication fluency\n\u2022    Must be legally authorized to work in India for any employer without sponsorship\n \n\n \nWhat will help you propel from the pack (Preferred Qualifications):\n\u2022    Advanced coursework or specialization in machine learning, artificial intelligence, applied statistics, or cloud computing. \n\u2022    Experience deploying Generative AI applications in a production or staging environment, particularly RAG or LLM-based workflows.\n\u2022    Relevant cloud, machine learning, or MLOps certification\n\u2022    Experience with RAGAS or TruLens; LangSmith or MLflow; regression, classification, ensemble methods, and common evaluation metrics; cloud platforms and cloud-based data environments such as AWS, Azure, or GCP.", "location": "Gurugram, Haryana, India", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://careers.united.com/us/en/c/corporate-jobs", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Ready for Review", "combinedDocStatus": "To be reviewed", "appliedOn": "8/25/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/25/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "", "hrEmail": "", "hrPhone": "", "reviewerNotes": "", "clNotes": "", "generalNotes": "", "aboutCompany": "Major global airline operating Digital Technology & Analytics center in Gurugram.", "resumeDriveId": "1b8O9Z4fjzyQ1V9huamQzT3FROQgdI-P0", "resumeLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "resumePreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clDriveId": "134_-e_1KRFXZGy8vzMJsvBw2VMDOadLU", "clLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clPreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "roleCategory": "operations_strategy", "extractedKeywords": "[object Object]", "revisionCount": 1, "clRevisionCount": 1, "resumeSections": {"summary_html": "<p>Senior Data &amp; Business Analyst combining extensive enterprise data analytics and operations intelligence experience with a strong foundation in commercial strategy and stakeholder consulting. Proven track record of architecting automated data pipelines and interactive KPI reporting suites using <strong>SQL, Python, and Tableau</strong> to stre