13 Mar 2022</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Resolved escalated consumer inquiries by utilizing <strong>CRM telemetry</strong> and historical performance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<div class=\"letter-meta\">\n  <div class=\"letter-date\">September 29, 2026</div>\n  <div class=\"recipient-block\">\n    <div>Hiring Manager</div>\n    <div>United</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"subject-line\"><strong>Re: Application for Analyst - Data Scientist</strong></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Analyst - Data Scientist role at United. What stood out to me in the job description is the focus on building practical data workflows and turning messy problems into clear solutions. Before spending the last five years in data analytics, I ran my own small business for ten years. That mix taught me how much time teams lose when numbers do not match across different tools. Fixing those gaps between business needs and technical teams is the part of the job I enjoy most.</p>\n<p>Outside of writing Python code and building models, I spend my free time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating small daily tasks with n8n. Growing mushrooms in North India's weather is not a fancy hobby. It comes down to watching basic details closely. If moisture or airflow slips even a little, the whole batch fails. I bring that same habit to my work when I check data quality, test workflows, or build reliable applications that leaders rely on.</p>\n<p>I also believe analysis is only useful when it solves a real problem on the ground. At Concentrix, our hiring data showed that new joiners were struggling once they started work. Sending another dashboard to management was not fixing the issue. I looked closely at the hiring steps and worked with leadership to bring our training team directly into the interview stage. That simple change improved hire quality by 84%. In my current role at Highspring India, I use the same practical approach across four engineering teams to automate recurring reports and cut manual work by 40%.</p>\n<p>My day-to-day work covers SQL, Python, and working closely with business and tech teams. If your team uses an internal tool I have not worked with yet, I learn new systems quickly. Practical challenges early in my career taught me how to stay resourceful and get things done without hand-holding. When I take ownership of a task, you will not have to follow up twice.</p>\n<p>I would welcome the chance to bring this steady, practical approach to your team. Thank you for your time and consideration, and I look forward to speaking with you soon.</p>"}, {"sNo": "9", "sNoNum": 9, "resumeId": "RES-9", "company": "United", "industry": "Airlines", "jobId": "Job IdGGN00002622", "title": "Senior Analyst - Finance Data Capability", "jd": "Description\nThis role sits at the intersection of Finance, Data, and AI, enabling the transformation of finance data into a strategic, intelligence-driven asset. It supports the design, governance, and activation of finance data capabilities to deliver faster insights, improved decision-making, and scalable business value.\n\nThe role will drive adoption of modern data platforms, while actively exploring and embedding GenAI and agentic solutions to automate workflows, enhance analytics, and enable intelligent, self-service finance operations. Working closely with Finance and Digital Technology teams, this position contributes to building an AI-enabled finance ecosystem that is standardized, efficient, and future-ready.\n\nJob Overview and Responsibilities\n\n1. Support Enterprise-Wide Data Standards, Analytics, and Insights\n\nSupport cross-functional collaborations to assess and redesign finance data processes and technical landscapes, focusing on simplification, standardization, and end-to-end optimization aligned with enterprise goals\nWork with large and complex (big) data sets across finance domains, ensuring scalable handling, efficient processing, and performance optimization across systems and data platforms\nEvaluate and embed GenAI and agentic solutions (e.g., copilots, autonomous workflows, intelligent pipelines) to reimagine finance processes, reduce manual effort, and accelerate decision-making cycles\nDrive adoption of modern data and automation tools (Data Platforms, Oracle, Alteryx, Tableau), augmenting them with AI-driven insights, predictive analytics, and intelligent automation\nDevelop and maintain financial data products, standardized KPIs, reusable datasets, and robust, dynamic data structures (e.g., scalable data models, semantic layers) to support evolving business needs and AI consumption\nMaintain and validate finance data mappings, transformation logic, and integrations, while exploring AI-assisted reconciliation, mapping automation, and anomaly detection\nSupport finance data governance by defining data quality rules and partnering on controls and lineage, leveraging AI for continuous monitoring, exception handling, and automated remediation insights\n2. Support financial transformation initiatives\n\nCollaborate cross-functionally to support finance data transformation initiatives, incorporating AI-first design principles, scalable data structures, and automation opportunities into solution architecture\n\nPartner with stakeholders (DT, Finance, etc.) to ensure alignment with enterprise strategy, including identification and prioritization of GenAI, agentic workflows, and big data use cases\n\nSupport delivery of transformation initiatives (milestones, timelines, reporting), while piloting and scaling agent-based workflows and AI-enabled process automation\n\nContribute to business cases by quantifying impact from AI, automation, and improved data architecture (e.g., scalability, speed, accuracy, and cost efficiency\n \n\nThis position is offered on local terms and conditions.  Expatriate assignments and sponsorship for employment visas, even on a time-limited visa status, will not be awarded. This position is for United Airlines Business Services Pvt. Ltd - a wholly owned subsidiary of United Airlines Inc.\n\nQualifications\nWhat\u2019s needed to succeed (Minimum Qualifications):\n\nBachelor's degree\nFinance, Accounting, Information Systems, Computer Science, or related field\n4+ years of finance and/or technology experience\nExperience in Finance Analytics, Data Analytics, Finance Systems, or Technology Transformation\nStrong expertise in finance data, reporting, analytics, data modeling, and master data governance\nExperience working with large, complex datasets using platforms such as Databricks, Snowflake, Foundry, SQL Server\nHands-on experience with Tableau and/or Tableau for reporting and visualization\nMust have working knowledge of Oracle EDM, complimentary would be Oracle ERP, Oracle EPM\nStrong proficiency in SQL and data analysis\nExperience using Python for analytics, automation, or process improvement\nExperience with Alteryx or similar ETL/data transformation tools\nFamiliarity with GenAI tools (e.g., Copilot, ChatGPT), AI-assisted analytics, and agentic workflows/intelligent automation\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills, with the ability to translate complex data into actionable business insights\nAbility to independently identify and implement opportunities to improve finance processes through data, automation, AI, and scalable technology solutions, AI, and scalable technology solutions\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to present complex data, AI-driven insights, and process improvements to both finance and non-finance stakeholders\nStrong understanding of how people, processes, data, and technology (including AI/automation) come together to build scalable and sustainable capabilities\nAbility to work independently and proactively identify opportunities to embed AI, automation, and improved data structures into existing workflows\n \nWhat will help you propel from the pack (Preferred Qualifications):\n\nMaster's degree\nMasters of Business Administration\nExperience in airline or similar industry\nExperience with PMO/project management tools such as Smartsheet, JIRA, or similar platforms\nUnderstanding of finance data standards, governance, controls, and business processes across domains such as GL, AP, AR, FP&A, and Treasury.\nExperience establishing or driving data definitions, business rules, and reporting standards across functions\nExposure to cloud-based data and analytics architectures (e.g., AWS Data Lake, Azure, or similar platforms).", "location": "Gurugram, Haryana, India", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://careers.united.com/us/en/c/corporate-jobs", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Not Created", "combinedDocStatus": "", "appliedOn": "8/25/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/25/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "reference": "", "h