 to ensure strict pricing & promotion reliability.</li>\n    <li>Partnered with 4+ cross-functional retail groups to deploy <strong>automation tools</strong>, accelerating feature deployment velocity and maintaining project quality of 95%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Leveraged advanced <strong>Excel</strong> models and statistical techniques to analyze workforce datasets, improving hire quality by 84%.</li>\n    <li>Maintained stringent <strong>data governance</strong> standards by automating upskilling project assessments, increasing team productivity by 25%.</li>\n    <li>Delivered targeted operational insights through rigorous <strong>metrics tracking</strong>, successfully resolving critical knowledge gaps across internal stakeholder groups.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Executed comprehensive <strong>market research</strong> for Wild Vitamin Drink's website development, resulting in a 25% increase in HORECA sales.</li>\n    <li>Partnered with IPL stakeholders on merchandise sponsorship strategies, driving a 15% increase in fan merchandise sales through targeted promotions.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<p class=\"salutation\"><strong>Dear Kankona Roy and the Hiring Team at 7-Eleven Global Solution Center,</strong></p>\n<p>What caught my attention about the <strong>Data Analyst</strong> role at 7-Eleven Global Solution Center is how directly the job description addresses the day-to-day realities of retail merchandising and category management: turning disparate sales, promotion, and vendor data into reliable baseline insights. Having spent the last several years translating messy operational workflows into clean SQL models and production dashboards\u2014preceded by a decade of running my own commercial operations\u2014I know that category growth depends entirely on accurate reporting and disciplined data reconciliation. That practical middle ground between business execution and data integrity is where I do my best work.</p>\n<p>When I am not writing <strong>SQL</strong> queries, mapping datasets, or building <strong>Tableau</strong> reports, I spend my spare time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating personal workflows with n8n. Cultivating mushrooms in North India\u2019s climate isn\u2019t a romantic hobby; it is an exercise in strict variable control\u2014if humidity, airflow, or substrate prep drifts even slightly, the batch fails. I bring that same practical stewardship to the systems I manage at work, whether I am validating retail metrics across systems, maintaining complex data sources, or translating ambiguous business requests into <strong>accurate, standardized reports</strong>.</p>\n<p>Furthermore, I believe data analysis is only as useful as the operational fix it drives. During my time at Concentrix, our workforce data kept flagging quality drops in new cohorts, and simply handing leadership another dashboard wasn't fixing the underlying issue. I dug into the recruitment funnel, traced the disconnect between initial screening and floor realities, and helped embed our training team directly into the hiring workflow, which drove an <strong>84% improvement in hire quality</strong>. I apply that same proactive rigor in my current role at Highspring India, partnering across multiple groups to profile 1M+ records, resolve data consistency issues, and cut manual reporting overhead by 40%.</p>\n<p>While my technical foundation covers strong ground across SQL, Python, BI reporting, and cross-functional data validation, I may not have hands-on experience with every specific proprietary system in your retail stack on day one. Early in my career, navigating real-world commercial and financial constraints taught me how to be resourceful, focus on fundamentals, and become a <strong>dedicated learner with a sharp focus</strong> on operational efficiency. Above all, I am unconditionally dependable\u2014when I take ownership of a deliverable, you will never have to chase me to see it through.</p>\n<p>I would value the chance to bring this grounded ownership, rigorous data validation, and steady execution to your merchandising and category management teams.</p><p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to discussing how my experience can support your upcoming analytics initiatives.</p>"}], "linkedin": [{"id": "LI-35", "date": "2026-10-06", "company": "Swiggy / Flipkart", "targetPerson": "Partho Sarathi Bhaduri (Manager People & BI Analytics, Swiggy)", "profileUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/partho-sarathi-bhaduri/", "postUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/partho-sarathi-bhaduri_ai-artificialintelligence-machinelearning-activity-7452733788888911872-gbOY", "actionType": "Post Comment", "topic": "Partho Sarathi Bhaduri on Power BI data modelling and AI-assisted analytics workflows at Swiggy", "draftedContent": "Solid modeling truly is the backbone of reliable AI analytics.", "approvalStatus": "Reworked & Rule Learned", "executionStatus": "Awaiting Approval"}, {"id": "LI-35", "date": "2026-10-06", "company": "Swiggy / Flipkart", "targetPerson": "Partho Sarathi Bhaduri (Manager People & BI Analytics, Swiggy)", "profileUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/partho-sarathi-bhaduri/", "postUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/partho-sarathi-bhaduri_ai-artificialintelligence-machinelearning-activity-7452733788888911872-gbOY", "actionType": "Post Comment", "topic": "Parth